# The collapsed sidebar (the reference's SidebarRailDots, D122996657..66):
# under the shelf, search as one more shelf row, a hairline, then one dot per
# thread Home lists -- top level only, no archived thread, no thread an
# automation started -- in list order. Dots are 10px on a 19px row, the whole
# rail width clickable; the column has a 10px slot above and below for an
# edge arrow, empty while every dot fits.
#
# The mock has 20 Home threads; two marked automation-born (t5, r9) drop out.
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark","sidebar_collapsed":true}
# env: HANABI_MOCK_AUTOMATION=t5,r9
require_thread t2
wait_frames 16
assert_ui rail_search x=14 h=30
assert_ui rail_rule x=0 w=52 h=1
assert_ui rail_arrow_slot_up h=10
assert_ui rail_dot_0 x=0 w=52 h=19
assert_ui rail_dot_17 h=19
expect_no_ui rail_dot_18
expect_no_ui rail_arrow_up
expect_no_ui rail_arrow_down
# A click opens that thread.
click_ui rail_dot_0
wait_frames 10
expect_text "profiling the disk"
